.TH focusforge-cli-sharpness-map 1  "sharpness-map 0.2.1" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-sharpness\-map \- Write the focus score of every frame of a stack, and of a composite, as maps on one scale
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli sharpness\-map\fR [\fB\-\-composite\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-priority\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-out\fR> <\fIDIR\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the focus score of every frame of a stack, and of a composite, as maps on one scale.
.PP
The scale is the 99th percentile of each pixel\*(Aqs peak focus score over the frames, so a value means the same sharpness in every map; a map holds the focus score divided by it, and a value above 1 is sharper than the scale. Frames are read without alignment; `\-\-composite` adds the composite\*(Aqs own focus score on the frames\*(Aq scale.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Directory the maps are written to; created if missing
.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR
A composite image of the frames\*(Aq size to map on the frames\*(Aq scale
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the scale and the written maps as one JSON object
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fI<PRIORITY>\fR [default: normal]
How many frames are read at once; the maps are the same at either value
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
low: One frame at a time, leaving the other cores to other work
.IP \(bu 2
normal: As many frames at once as the host has threads
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDIR\fR>
Directory of frames to map (non\-recursive, descending into a `frames` subdirectory)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
